{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.WeightedChebyshev","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WeightedChebyshev","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Chebyshev","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Monovary","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WeightedChebyshev.weighted_cov_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WeightedChebyshev.weighted_cov_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WeightedChebyshev.lean#L110-L117","doc":"The form the covariance argument uses: with a weight summing to `1`, the\nweighted covariance of two monovarying observables is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WeightedChebyshev.monovaryOn_pairwise_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WeightedChebyshev.monovaryOn_pairwise_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WeightedChebyshev.lean#L95-L108","doc":"`MonovaryOn` gives the pairwise condition the inequality above wants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WeightedChebyshev.weighted_chebyshev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WeightedChebyshev.weighted_chebyshev","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WeightedChebyshev.lean#L75-L93","doc":"**Chebyshev's association inequality, weighted.**\n\nIf `w ≥ 0` on `s` and every pair satisfies `(fᵢ − fⱼ)(gᵢ − gⱼ) ≥ 0` — which is\nwhat it means for `f` and `g` to vary together — then\n\n    (∑ w f) * (∑ w g)  ≤  (∑ w) * (∑ w f g).\n\nThe pair condition is stated directly rather than through `MonovaryOn` so the\ntheorem can be applied without a `LinearOrder`; `monovaryOn_pairwise_nonneg`\nbelow converts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WeightedChebyshev.two_mul_weighted_cov_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WeightedChebyshev.two_mul_weighted_cov_eq","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WeightedChebyshev.lean#L51-L73","doc":"The symmetrisation identity. Both sides are `2 ·` the weighted covariance,\nwritten once as a double sum of pair differences and once in closed form. ","signatureChunk":0}]}